From e1fed238c22f7011f8a1a4fe33389a796c6cf1e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blue Cuenca <blue.cuenca@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 02:14:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: fix use-after-free and double-free in
 aicwf_process_rxframes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the USB aggregate RX path (aicwf_usb_rx_aggr=true), when pkt_len > 1600
is detected inside the inner while(aicwf_another_ptk(skb)) loop, the code
freed the container skb with dev_kfree_skb() then used continue, which
re-evaluated the inner loop condition on the freed skb.

This caused a use-after-free read in aicwf_another_ptk(), and if the freed
memory still appeared to contain packet data, the loop body would execute
again on the freed skb. If that iteration hit the config packet path and
kmalloc failed, aicwf_dev_skb_free() would be called on the already-freed
skb, triggering:

  refcount_t: underflow; use-after-free
  sk_skb_reason_drop -> aicwf_process_rxframes

The premature atomic_dec() also caused rx_cnt to go out of sync,
contributing to the "rxq is over flow" errors seen in parallel.

Fix: replace dev_kfree_skb + atomic_dec + continue with break, letting
the outer loop's existing dev_kfree_skb + atomic_dec (lines 787-788)
perform the single correct cleanup of the container skb.

This affects the AIC8800D80 on LonganPi 3H — despite the device name,
it reports USB PID 0x8d81 which sets aicwf_usb_rx_aggr=true.

Signed-off-by: Blue Cuenca <blue.cuenca@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_txrxif.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_txrxif.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_txrxif.c
index 2b9ebf4bf..66b0cb386 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_txrxif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_txrxif.c
@@ -730,9 +730,8 @@ int aicwf_process_rxframes(struct aicwf_rx_priv *rx_priv)
 	        pkt_len = (*skb->data | (*(skb->data + 1) << 8));
 	        //printk("p:%d, s:%d , %x\n", pkt_len, skb->len, data[2]);
 	        if (pkt_len > 1600) {
-	            dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-	            atomic_dec(&rx_priv->rx_cnt);
-	                continue;
+	            txrx_err("pkt_len > 1600, dropping container skb\n");
+	            break;
 	        }
 
 	        if((skb->data[2] & USB_TYPE_CFG) != USB_TYPE_CFG) { // type : data
-- 
2.17.1

